==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mother Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Beefcake Cat''' when obtained from [[Actress Awakens!]] (may drop on the first stage but guaranteed on the second) when it is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
It is not recommended to purchase this cat until you've unlocked Talents. Roll the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] instead for a chance to get its stronger variant, [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]]. However, if you do purchase this cat, be aware that it is only useful very early on, prior to obtaining Salon, or very late, if heavily talented. Use it alongside meatshields in stages with plenty of money available to build up a stack and deliver high DPS from a distance.

It also has some great [[Cat Combo|combos]] like [[Arm Day Everyday (Combo)|Arm Day Everyday]], a 4-slot defense combo.

==='''True Form'''===
By the time you unlock Beefcake cat, you'll probably have Paris Cat, meaning that there is no real reason to use this unit. While you can expect to True Form Paris Cat and give her + levels, Beefcake is stuck with much lower damage and no chance to convert dupes into extra levels, which will widen the gap over time.

==='''Talents'''===
Beefcake Cat <u>absolutely needs</u> the boost from his health and damage up Talents in order to be usable, as his stats will not be relevant late-game otherwise. After and only after unlocking those, consider unlocking Immune to Surge, a more unique than rare trait for a replaceable attacker which will become very relevant in late game when said threats become prominent. Strengthen is also a nice addition, further increasing his attack power. Slow Resist is expensive and situational, thus not recommended.

With all of this in mind, there is little reason to invest into Beefcake Cat's Talents thanks to [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]], whose own Talents provide Surge Immunity, but for a unit with far better stats that remain viable throughout the whole game.

